# The shut door: the one decision the whole game is built on.
#
#     build\RatnaBay.exe --yard --script Docs\scripts\clip-door.rbs
#     powershell -File tools\make-clips.ps1
#
# This is the clip to lead with. Not the prettiest seconds in the game, but the only
# ones that show what it *is*: a room cleared, a pot you are holding, and a door
# that will not tell you what is behind it.
#
# Scripted rather than performed, and that is the point. Footage captured by hand
# has to be re-performed every time the art changes and never comes back quite the
# same. This regenerates identically, from any machine, in one command.
#
# The HUD stays on. It is not clutter here -- health, the pot and the stones at
# risk are the numbers the decision is made with, and a clip of the decision with
# the numbers hidden is a clip of a man looking at a door.

# Same seed and the same route as walk.rbs, which is the one sequence in the repo
# that is known to reach room one on foot rather than through a wall.
descend 1 20789
wait 1.5

look 0 0
walk 4
use
wait 0.5

# Recording starts once the door is open, so the clip opens on movement rather than
# on somebody standing still reading a prompt.
record captures/clip-door 12 30

# Down the corridor and into the room.
walk 4.5

# Let them come. A bandit closes from seven metres to two in about a second and a
# half, and swinging before it arrives is what the first attempt at this clip did:
# twelve swings, one miss, eleven refused by the cooldown, and no fight on screen.
god on
wait 1.4

# Swung one at a time with the cooldown respected. `swing 12` in a single frame
# reports eleven refusals and shows one animation; a sword swings every 0.45s and
# the clip should look like somebody fighting rather than like somebody mashing.
#
# These swings do not connect, and that is a known fault rather than a staging
# choice: a console swing runs in PumpScript, which is earlier in Update than the
# encounter, so Encounter.Focused is not what the crosshair is on by the time
# PlayerAttack reads it. A bandit standing 2.1m dead ahead inside a 2.4m reach is
# missed every time. It does not hurt the footage -- a miss still swings the
# weapon and still makes the sound -- but it is on the board to fix.
swing 1
wait 0.5
swing 1
wait 0.5
swing 1
wait 0.5
swing 1
wait 0.5

# The room resolved. Not how a player would do it, and the only staged beat in the
# clip: what follows is the panel, and the panel is what this is for.
kill all
wait 3.5

quit
